      "number": 38,
      "title": "OPS-003 | DOCUMENTATION TASK | Create server-validation operating pack",
      "body": "# OPS-003 DOCUMENTATION TASK — Server Validation Operating Pack\n\n**Parent Mission:** #12  \n**Related Execution:** #37  \n**Knowledge Systems Lead:** @bmobinacs  \n**Technical Validator:** @zacharymeyer-IT\n\n## Gap\n\nOPS-003 requires a repeatable Server Validation Runbook, individual validation-record template, and backlog/disposition tracker, but those controlled artifacts do not currently exist on `main`. The current server work must generate durable operational records rather than remain in verbal updates or scattered Issue comments.\n\n## Objective\n\nCreate the minimum controlled documentation needed to support the current pilot and future server intake:\n\n1. **OPS-003 Server Validation Runbook**\n2. **Individual Server Validation Record Template**\n3. **Initial Server Backlog and Disposition Tracker**\n4. **Short station startup/shutdown and handoff checklist**\n\n## Required Content\n\nThe documentation must preserve the safety and authorization boundaries in #12, including:\n\n- observation and non-destructive discovery first;\n- one-server-at-a-time identity control;\n- required hardware/software-state evidence;\n- clear distinction between power-on, POST, hardware detection, diagnostic result, and overall disposition;\n- stop conditions for data, ownership, electrical, lifting/transport, network, or destructive-action concerns;\n- no wipe, reimage, firmware, BIOS, RAID, storage, production-network, disposal, or deployment action without explicit authorization;\n- approved disposition categories and next-action ownership;\n- operator, validator, date, and evidence references.\n\n## Change-Control Workflow\n\n1. Use a dedicated documentation branch.\n2. Mobina drafts the operating pack from the current pilot experience.\n3. Zach validates the technical sequence against actual station use.\n4. Record ambiguities or safety gaps in this Issue before revising around them.\n5. Open one pull request linking this Issue and #12.\n6. Request Mission Owner review before merge.\n7. After merge, use the canonical tracker for the current server backlog and link the completed records from #37.\n\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- All four artifacts exist in a discoverable OPS-003 location.\n- The runbook matches what the station can actually support.\n- The validation template captures every minimum record field in #12.\n- The backlog tracker contains the current servers and their states.\n- Zach's technical validation is recorded.\n- The pull request is approved and merged.\n- The final artifact locations are linked back to #12.\n",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-22T20:25:03Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/student-operated-technology-ecosystem/SOTE-framework/issues/38",
