      "number": 4,
      "title": "OPS-002 | MISSION ISSUE | Mission Thermal Shield | Environmental Baseline",
      "body": "# OPS-002 MISSION ISSUE — Mission Thermal Shield\n\n**Domain:** Infrastructure  \n**Execution Role:** SOTE Infrastructure Operator  \n**Mission Owner:** Professor Michael Rinsem  \n**Priority:** High — Initial Mission Control commissioning work  \n**Objective:** Establish a defensible baseline of Mission Control power, cooling, and thermal behavior before the environment is placed under sustained load.\n\n> **Live operational state:** GitHub fields are authoritative. **Assignees** identify the current Operator(s); the **status label** identifies current mission state; **comments** are the chronological work log. Do not duplicate live staffing or status in this mission charter.\n\n## What do I do first?\n\n1. **Read this entire Mission Issue before beginning work.**\n2. **Complete the Pre-Flight Checklist below.** Do not begin equipment work until all required Pre-Flight items are confirmed.\n3. **Then open and read the OPS-002 Runbook.** [Open OPS-002 RUNBOOK — Mission Thermal Shield](https://github.com/student-operated-technology-ecosystem/SOTE-framework/blob/main/implementations/ccac/mission-control/operations/OPS-002_Mission-Thermal-Shield_v1.0.md)\n4. Post `MISSION STARTED` or `MISSION RESUMED — Current starting point` before equipment work begins.\n5. Post `CHECKPOINT — What was completed — Result/findings — Next step` after meaningful phases or significant findings.\n6. If work cannot safely continue, post `BLOCKED — What happened — What is needed to continue` and set the Issue status label to the appropriate waiting/blocked state.\n7. When execution is complete, request independent validation from another assigned Operator when available: `READY FOR VALIDATION — Work completed — Evidence/report location — Remaining concerns — @validator`.\n8. The validating Operator records either `VALIDATION COMPLETE — What was reviewed — Result` or `VALIDATION FAILED — Discrepancy/findings — Required next action`.\n9. After successful validation, request Mission Owner review with `READY FOR REVIEW — Validation complete — Evidence/report location — Remaining concerns — @ProfRinsem`.\n\nGitHub automatically records comment author and timestamp. Use `@username` only when intentionally handing work to or calling the attention of a specific person.\n\n## Runbook\n\n[**Open OPS-002 RUNBOOK — Mission Thermal Shield**](https://github.com/student-operated-technology-ecosystem/SOTE-framework/blob/main/implementations/ccac/mission-control/operations/OPS-002_Mission-Thermal-Shield_v1.0.md)\n\n**Mission Issue = stable mission charter and operational work queue.**  \n**Runbook = how to perform the technical work.**  \n**GitHub fields = live staffing and mission state.**  \n**Comments = chronological execution, validation, blocker, and handoff record.**\n\n## Pre-Flight Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have read this entire Mission Issue.\n- [ ] I have read the OPS-002 runbook.\n- [ ] I understand which equipment may be powered or observed during this mission.\n- [ ] Required measurement tools are available.\n- [ ] Current equipment and power state have been recorded before changes are made.\n- [ ] I understand the Stop-Work Conditions below.\n- [ ] I know who to contact if the mission becomes blocked or unsafe.\n\nIf any required item cannot be confirmed, do not proceed. Post a `BLOCKED` comment explaining what is missing or unclear.\n\n## Mission Deliverables\n\n- [ ] Initial room, rack-intake, and rack-exhaust baseline recorded.\n- [ ] Equipment/load state documented with measurements.\n- [ ] Controlled phased power-up observations completed where approved and safe.\n- [ ] Available UPS/PDU information and equipment health observations recorded.\n- [ ] Mission Thermal Shield Field Report completed.\n- [ ] Environmental/power concerns identified and documented.\n- [ ] Follow-up Issues created for work that cannot be completed within this mission.\n- [ ] Initial low-cost sensor requirements/recommendations documented for the next monitoring phase.\n- [ ] Independent validation recorded when another qualified Operator is available.\n\n## Safety / Stop-Work Conditions\n\n**Safety takes priority over mission completion.** Stop work and document the condition if equipment generates a thermal, power, fan, or PSU alarm; temperature rises unexpectedly or rapidly; airflow appears obstructed or inadequate; equipment shuts down or repeatedly resets; electrical or power behavior appears unsafe; continuing would require work outside authorized scope; or you are uncertain whether continuing is safe.\n\nDo not perform electrical work outside authorized scope.\n\n## Mission Complete\n\nAfter execution and validation are complete, post:\n\n`READY FOR REVIEW — Validation complete — Evidence/report location — Remaining concerns — @ProfRinsem`\n\nThe Mission Owner verifies the work log, Field Report, evidence, validation, and follow-up Issues, then either requests additional work or closes the Mission Issue.\n\n## Change Control\n\nIf field experience shows that the runbook or other controlled SOTE documentation is incorrect or incomplete, **do not silently rewrite the official document**. Document the finding in this Mission Issue. Controlled documentation changes should follow the established GitHub branch, pull request, review, and merge workflow.",
