      "number": 26,
      "title": "Infrastructure onboarding: review SOTE Operations and Mission Control",
      "body": "@mikebandes — welcome to the SOTE GitHub workflow.\n\nWe have formalized the SOTE Operations architecture, including the Infrastructure domain and your role as **SOTE Infrastructure Operator**.\n\nCanonical document:\n`framework/01-sote-operations-architecture.md`\n\nYour Infrastructure lane includes Mission Control, switching/routing, racks, cabling/patching, Rocket's Forge, Patch Bay Alpha, Rocket's Engineering Bay, and related physical/network infrastructure work.\n\nOnce repository access is enabled, please use this Issue as your starting point:\n1. Read the Infrastructure and Mission Control sections of the architecture document.\n2. Review the Issue workflow so you can see how infrastructure work will be coordinated in GitHub.\n3. Leave a comment here with any question, correction, or infrastructure observation you have.\n\nThis is not a Knowledge Systems/documentation assignment. GitHub is being used here as the operating environment for the infrastructure work you participate in.",
