      "number": 1,
      "title": "Future Work: CCAC SOTE physical field verification and source-of-truth reconciliation",
      "body": "## Parked for future work\n\nThe Google Drive archaeology/migration audit for the core CCAC SOTE infrastructure is substantially complete. The next phase should be performed physically in CEIT 325 with the racks and devices available.\n\n## Field verification scope\n\n- [ ] R1-SW01 — identify hardware, RU, cabling, current configuration, VLAN/interface state; reconcile wipe/recommission lineage.\n- [ ] R1-SW02 — capture current hardware/configuration and validate commissioned state.\n- [ ] R1-SW03 — capture current hardware/configuration and validate role/state.\n- [ ] R1-DIST01 — verify existence, hardware, rack position, configuration, and R1↔R2 distribution/trunk path.\n- [ ] R2-AGG01 — verify hardware/model/serial/RU, management state, VLAN 120, SVI, trunks, neighbors, startup/running-config consistency.\n- [ ] R2-PVE01 — verify hardware, storage, NIC mapping, Proxmox version, management addressing, VM inventory, and service state.\n- [ ] R2-PVE02 / R2-PVE03 — inventory and determine actual commissioned state.\n- [ ] Verify physical Rack 1 and Rack 2 elevations against PHYS-001 v1.1.\n- [ ] Verify Rack 3 against the later v1.2 Exact Template elevation.\n- [ ] Verify Patch Bay Alpha and replace draft elevation with an as-built record.\n- [ ] Photograph rack fronts/rears and record RU positions, cable paths, uplinks, labels, power/PDU paths, serial/service tags where appropriate.\n\n## Service verification\n\nDetermine whether these legacy Rocket's Forge services actually exist and whether they remain part of the current architecture:\n\n- [ ] R2-DHCP01\n- [ ] R2-WEB01\n- [ ] R2-HDSK01 — reconcile against current ACE/GLPI cloud direction.\n- [ ] R2-IPAM01 — NetBox.\n- [ ] R2-OBS01 — monitoring/Uptime Kuma.\n- [ ] R2-MGMT01 — administrative jump box.\n- [ ] Maintenance Gateway / External Access Boundary — determine whether still needed and verify that no CCAC production-network transit is introduced.\n\n## Source-of-truth completion\n\n- [ ] Capture sanitized device configuration snapshots into GitHub.\n- [ ] Do not commit credentials, secrets, tokens, private keys, SNMP credentials, or password hashes.\n- [ ] Deploy/validate NetBox if R2-IPAM01 is not operational.\n- [ ] Populate NetBox only with reconciled current devices, racks, interfaces, cables, VLANs, prefixes, IPs, and services.\n- [ ] Update GitHub as-built summaries from verified field state.\n- [ ] Preserve legacy Drive documents as provenance/history rather than deleting them.\n\n## Evidence hierarchy\n\n**current field observation/device output > later commissioning/as-built evidence > approved command reference/standard > proposal/design > draft > superseded artifact**\n\n## Completion condition\n\nClose this issue when the physical CCAC SOTE implementation has been field-verified and GitHub + NetBox accurately represent the current as-built environment.",
